   "etymology": "Borrowed from Late Latin cellārium (“cellar, pantry”). For the ending compare hamshor, fruer, etc. Doublet of qilar.\nDiscarded theories\nMeyer (1891) separately misidentifies Bardhi's chiuer a typographical mistake for qiler and hesitatingly compares qur with ahur. Jokl (1923) connects the word to descendants of Proto-Slavic *klětь (“barn, cellar”) and other descendants of Proto-Indo-European *ḱley- (“to shelter, cover”). Çabej SEFSH [1950s–1980] compares it to the descendants of Proto-Celtic *kladeti (“to dig, bury”). Orel (1998) tentatively compares it to qos (“to finish”).",
